1
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:09,800
You are particularly interested in extremes:

2
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:15,920
Microscopic organisms that live under extreme conditions-

3
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:20,200
-like the ice on Antarctic or inside volcanoes.

4
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:27,560
These environments are similar to those on other planets, such as Mars.

5
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:34,000
It is important partly to understand how life has arisen on our planet-

6
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:39,440
-And what conditions we have to colonize other celestial bodies.

7
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:45,400
Some day our own planet will be swallowed by the universe again.

8
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:51,680
It can be through an asteroid, as on the time of dinosaurs-

9
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:54,040
-or that the sun goes out.

10
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:59,400
No man has yet set foot on Mars, the race is underway.

11
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:04,600
Natuschka Lee is researching the European Space Organization Esa-

12
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:09,960
-It to demonstrate life in space in general and Mars in particular-

13
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:14,480
-Ope which life from the earth can survive there.

14
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:19,480
We have sent different organisms to the space station.

15
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:25,040
There have been extreme bacteria, fungi, lichens and mosses.

16
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:30,480
They have been sitting on a container that we attached outside the space station.

17
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:35,800
Then they have been allowed to circulate around the earth for 1.5 years.

18
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:41,600
So we hope to simulate how organisms from the earth can react-

19
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:47,720
-Or genuine space conditions, e.g.
If they ended up on Mars.

20
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:51,080
Many survived cosmic radiation-
